"OOPSLA paper","target":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.24054","line":52},{"title":"PDF","target":"https://www.ijcai.org/Proceedings/73/Papers/027B.pdf","line":139},{"title":"PDF","target":"https://erlang.org/download/armstrong_thesis_2003.pdf","line":140},{"title":"PDF","target":"https://mariachris.github.io/Pubs/PADL-2010.pdf","line":141},{"title":"PDF","target":"https://mariachris.github.io/Pubs/TFP-2011.pdf","line":142},{"title":"arXiv","target":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.24054","line":143},{"title":"pobox: External buffer processes to protect against mailbox overflow in Erlang","target":"https://github.com/ferd/pobox","line":144},{"title":"Blog post","target":"https://ferd.ca/handling-overload.html","line":145}],"metadata":{"title":"The Isolation Trap","source":"https://causality.blog/essays/the-isolation-trap/","author":["[[Causality]]"],"published":null,"created":"2026-03-14","description":"Erlang's mailbox design is more disciplined than Go's channels: only the owning process can read from a mailbox, and sends are asynchronous. Yet the four failure modes of shared mutable state still show up, just in different shapes.","tags":["#causality","#mpi","#mutability"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[[38,48]],"key":"Clippings/The Isolation Trap.md"},
